  </div>
</Chapter>

<!-- ================= 16 REFLECTION ================= -->
<Chapter id="reflect" num="16" title="Outcome and reflection: what we built, and what I learned" tone="mint">
  <div class="grid g2 reveal">
    <div class="card ink">
      <h3>Outcome</h3>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>A shared café table where four people each choose their height</li>
        <li>Estimated cost of ₹17.5k, against ₹1.8 lakh for the closest accessible competitor</li>
        <li>Compact: about 0.79 m², the footprint of a 1 m round table</li>
        <li>Strength checked by FEA and hand calculation; suction base tested physically</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card ink">
      <h3>What I learned</h3>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><b>Role-playing objects works.</b> Platini the plate surfaced hygiene issues no survey question asked about.</li>
        <li><b>Converge with several methods.</b> Seven decision methods agreeing made the choice easy to defend.</li>
        <li><b>Contradictions spark ideas.</b> “Everyone shares one height” turned into four quarters.</li>
        <li><b>Next:</b> a full-scale working prototype tested with real diners at the café.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="box-quote reveal">“Essentially, all models are wrong, but some are useful.” <span>— George E. P. Box</span></p>
</Chapter>

